title: elaboration
pid: f4d1c141-428e-4ae2-a683-295126acdea5
body: |2-
  Suppose you took notes on a book,
  collected under a note with title equal to the book's.
  Then you integrate that knowledge into your graph.
  From each of those integrated bits,
  the source appears in its containerward ancestry.
  I usually don't want that -- I want to see the source as content, not container.
  A command to reverse the direction of a contains relationship
  would make it easy to clean such data -- run from a child,
  it makes the child contain its parent,
  and removes the child from the parent.
